  </div>
</nav>

<header class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Life-Sign &amp; Distress Detection Wearable</span>
        <h1>She can't always<br>call for help.<br><em>Her band can.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">Safe Trace Band is a hard-wired safety wearable that quietly confirms a girl is alive and narrows down where to look — without a phone signal, without the internet, without a sound.</p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a href="#how" class="btn btn-primary">See How It Works</a>
          <a href="#contact" class="btn btn-ghost">Partner With Us</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="device-card">
        <div class="device-photo">
          <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Safe Trace Band wearable — black and purple wristband with a shield-check logo, showing the hidden panic button and rear sensor array">
        </div>
        <div class="device-info">
          <div class="vitals-head">
            <span class="vitals-title">Wearer Status</span>
            <span class="vitals-live">Monitoring</span>
          </div>
          <div class="readouts">
            <div class="readout"><div class="val">78</div><div class="lab">Heart Rate</div></div>
            <div class="readout"><div class="val">36.6°</div><div class="lab">Body Temp</div></div>
            <div class="readout"><div class="val amber">GSM</div><div class="lab">Signal</div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="vitals-foot">
            <span>No audio · No video</span>
            <span>Base station linked</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="wave-divider">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1160 34" preserveAspectRatio="none">
      <path d="M0 17 L1160 17" stroke="rgba(245,242,249,0.14)" stroke-width="1"/>
      <path d="M480 17 L500 17 L508 4 L518 30 L528 17 L560 17" stroke="#39B54A" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/>
    </svg>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="problem" id="problem">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--purple-deep);">The Gap</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">When a girl disappears, the first hours matter most — and that's exactly when families and rescuers know the least.</h2>
    <div class="problem-grid">
      <div class="problem-text">
        <p>Abduction of school girls remains a serious threat across rural and semi-urban communities in Nigeria. When it happens, families and security agencies are usually left without any timely information about a victim's location or condition, which delays the search from the very first hour.</p>
        <p>Most existing safety tools depend on a mobile phone and an internet connection — both of which are frequently unavailable, confiscated, or simply out of range during a hostage situation. Safe Trace Band was built around that exact failure point.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-block">
        <div class="stat"><div class="n">0</div><div class="d">Internet connections required to operate</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="n">GSM / RF</div><div class="d">Communication that works where mobile data doesn't</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="n">Discreet</div><div class="d">A distress trigger a captor cannot easily detect</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="how" id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">How It Works</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Five quiet steps between danger and rescue.</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">The band runs continuously in the background of a normal school day, and only acts when something is genuinely wrong.</p>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><div class="step-num">01</div><div class="step-body"><h3>Worn discreetly</h3><p>The band sits like an ordinary wrist accessory — nothing about its appearance suggests it's a safety device.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-num">02</div><div class="step-body"><h3>Continuous life-sign monitoring</h3><p>Heart rate, body temperature, and movement patterns are tracked quietly in the background, all day, every day.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-num">03</div><div class="step-body"><h3>Distress detection</h3><p>An abnormal life-sign pattern, or a secret manual trigger from the wearer, flags a possible emergency.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-num">04</div><div class="step-body"><h3>Silent signal transmission</h3><p>Using GSM or radio frequency — no internet required — the band sends the last known location and life-sign status to a base station.</p></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-num">05</div><div class="step-body"><h3>Rescue, guided</h3><p>Responders start their search already knowing she's alive, and roughly where to look — turning a blind search into a targeted one.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="hardware" id="hardware">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--purple-deep);">The Hardware</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">One band. A hidden trigger. Sensors that never stop reading.</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Every part of Safe Trace Band is built to stay unnoticed until the moment it's needed.</p>
    <div class="hardware-card">
      <div class="hardware-photo-wrap">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Safe Trace Band wearable with close-up call-outs of the hidden panic button on the strap and the heart rate sensor, temperature sensor, and charging ports on the back">
      </div>
      <div class="hardware-legend">
        <div class="item"><span class="dot"></span>Hidden panic button, built into the strap</div>
        <div class="item"><span class="dot"></span>Heart rate + temperature sensors on the back</div>
        <div class="item"><span class="dot"></span>Charging ports for daily top-up</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="features" id="features">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--purple-deep);">Built For Real Conditions</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Designed for the places where connectivity gives out first.</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid">
      <div class="feat">
        <svg class="fico" viewBox="0 0 30 30" fill="none"><circle cx="15" cy="15" r="12" stroke="#39B54A" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M15 8v7l5 3" stroke="#39B54A" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        <h3>Works offline, always</h3>
        <p>Runs entirely on GSM/RF signal, so it keeps working in rural and low-connectivity areas where phone apps fail.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <svg class="fico" viewBox="0 0 30 30" fill="none"><path d="M15 4l10 5v6c0 7-4.5 10.5-10 12-5.5-1.5-10-5-10-12V9l10-5z" stroke="#39B54A" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none"/></svg>
        <h3>No audio, no video</h3>
        <p>The device only reads vitals and location — never recording sound or footage, by design and by policy.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <svg class="fico" viewBox="0 0 30 30" fill="none"><path d="M6 22V13l9-8 9 8v9h-6v-6h-6v6z" stroke="#F5A623" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        <h3>Confirms she's alive</h3>
        <p>Heart rate and temperature readings give rescuers confirmation of life-sign status, not just a blinking dot on a map.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <svg class="fico" viewBox="0 0 30 30" fill="none"><path d="M15 3v24M6 8l18 14M24 8L6 22" stroke="#39B54A" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        <h3>Discreet distress trigger</h3>
        <p>A hidden manual trigger lets a wearer signal danger without a captor noticing any change in behavior.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <svg class="fico" viewBox="0 0 30 30" fill="none"><rect x="9" y="4" width="12" height="22" rx="3" stroke="#39B54A" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="12" y="9" width="6" height="9" fill="#39B54A"/></svg>
        <h3>Built to last the day</h3>
        <p>Low-power hardware keeps the band monitoring through a full school day and journey home.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feat">
        <svg class="fico" viewBox="0 0 30 30" fill="none"><path d="M4 15h5l2-7 4 14 3-9 2 5h6" stroke="#E1483C" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        <h3>Narrows the search area</h3>
        <p>Last known location plus vitals turns a wide, blind search into a focused rescue effort from hour one.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="privacy">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Privacy, By Design</span>
    <blockquote>No audio. No video. Just a signal that says <span>she's alive</span>, and here's where.</blockquote>
    <p class="note">Safe Trace Band was built to protect, not to surveil — it reads life signs and location only, in line with ethical and privacy standards for wearable safety technology.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="team" id="team">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="team-badge">KSH FOUNDATION EVERY GIRL 3.0</div>
    <h2>Designed and built by JOY MASOYI OF PRIME ACADEMY GOMBE</h2>
    <p>Safe Trace Band is a student-led hardware innovation from Prime Academy Gombe, developed to show how young girls can use ICT and engineering to solve real security problems in their own communities.</p>
    <div class="team-names"><strong>Team Digital Sentinels</strong> — Prime Academy Gombe, Gombe State, Nigeria</div>
  </div>
</section>

<footer id="contact">
  <div class="wrap">
